      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should pass the UUID in the opening request. Connecting a service on top of RFCOMM indeed requires a ServiceClassIDList and a ProtocolDescriptorList, but in our case, for simplicity, I think we should limit ourselves to the Serial Port Profile (SPP, which is already the UUID you\u0027re using on the python side), which is based on RFCOMM. \n\nIn this case, we should also rename this interface to `spp.proto` rather than `rfcomm.proto` and the service accordingly.",
